{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>ויזעקו</b> — The poet mentioned this because those who stray in the wilderness are not helped by those who know the roads or by diviners, only by crying out to HaShem — He alone can deliver them. Similarly, the imprisoned — no people in the world can help until HaShem decrees. So too the sick — no physicians can help them, only HaShem alone. And so the sailors and seafarers — all their wisdom shall be swallowed up."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 107, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:59.497544791Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}